{
  "about": "The website address a new dealership types, and the origin Lot Sync keeps for it (dealerships.website_origin, the key the extension syncs under), or null when the address is refused. One table for both copies of the rule: create_dealership's SQL (supabase/migrations/0007_signup.sql, checked by supabase/tests/signup.sql) and websiteOrigin() in manager/data.js (checked by test/manager.test.js). Rules: trim; no scheme means https; only http and https; host lower-cased, one trailing dot dropped; path, query and fragment dropped; the scheme's default port dropped and any other port refused; refused: user info, IP addresses, localhost, a host without a dot, a label that is empty, longer than 63 characters, starts or ends with a hyphen, or holds anything but a-z, 0-9 and hyphens (so a non-ASCII host is refused: the browser's address bar shows it, but the origin the extension sees is the xn-- form).",
